\p
\v 1 \add ≈Some¦147612 time afterwards¦147597,\add* David's¦147603 son¦147601 Amnon¦147609 \add ≈fell in love¦147608 with his beautiful¦147605 half-sister\add* Tamar¦147607 (Abshalom's¦147600 sister),
\v 2 and¦147623 \add *he\add* \add ≈made¦147616 himself¦147616 frustrated¦147614,\add* \add always thinking about her\add* because¦147617 she¦147622 was¦147614 a virgin¦147621. However¦147618, \add *he\add* \add ≈couldn't do¦147626 anything¦147628 with¦147617 her\add*.
\v 3 \add ≈But¦147630\add* Amnon¦147639 had a very¦147642 shrewd¦147641 friend¦147631 called Yonadab¦147633 (son¦147634 of¦147634 David's¦147638 brother¦147637 Shimeah¦147636)
\v 4 and¦147658 \add @Yonadab¦147657\add* \add ≈asked\add* him¦147645, “\add Hey,\add* \add ≈you're a son¦147650 of¦147650 the¦147652 king¦147652, so tell¦147656 me¦147657 why¦147646 you're always so unhappy\add*?”
\p “I'm¦147667 in¦147653 love¦147668 with¦147653 my¦147666 brother¦147666 Abshalom's¦147665 sister¦147664 Tamar¦147663,” Amnon¦147660 \add ≈replied¦147644\add*.
\p
\v 5 “\add ≈Go to bed¦147676\add* and pretend¦147677 to be sick¦147677,” Yonadab¦147672 \add ≈suggested\add*. “Then¦147670 \add when\add* your¦147679 father¦147679 comes¦147678 to see¦147680 you¦147680, \add ≈ask\add* him¦147682, ‘Please¦147684 let¦147683 my sister¦147686 Tamar¦147685 come¦147683 \add ≈to look after my food¦147693. She¦147689 can cook it here and serve it to me¦147687\add*.’ ”
\v 6 \add ≈So¦147700\add* Amnon lay¦147700 down¦147700 and pretended¦147702 to be sick¦147702, and \add when\add* the¦147704 king¦147704 came¦147703 to see¦147705 him, Amnon \add ≈asked\add* \add *him\add*, “Please¦147713, let¦147711 my¦147715 sister¦147715 Tamar¦147714 come¦147711 and make¦147716 a couple of¦147717 bread¦147716 rolls \add ≈while I'm watching, and then¦147700 she can serve them to me\add*.”
