\v 32 Then Yonadab¦148227 (David's¦148234 brother¦148232 Shimeah's¦148231 son¦148229) \add ≈spoke¦148226 up\add*, “My¦148239 master¦148239, don't¦148236 \add ≈imagine that\add* all¦148241 those young¦148243 men¦148243, the¦148244 king's¦148246 sons¦148244, have¦148247 been murdered¦148247. \add I suspect that\add* only Amnon¦148250 is dead, because¦148248 Abshalom¦148258 \add ≈has¦148247 been determined¦148260 to do this ever since\add* his¦148265 sister¦148265 Tamar¦148264 was humiliated.
\v 33 \add ≈So¦148267 my¦148271 master¦148271, don't¦148268 believe the¦148272 report that all¦148278 your\add* sons¦148280 are dead. \add ≈It's¦148288 probably\add* only Amnon¦148287 who's dead.
