\p
\v 1 \add ≈Now\add* Yoav¦148399 (Tseruyah's¦148402 son¦148400) \add ≈realised\add* that¦148403 the¦148405 king¦148406 \add ≈missed\add* Abshalom¦148409,
\v 2 \add ≈so\add* he¦148411 sent¦148411 for a wise¦148417 woman from¦148415 Tekoa¦148413 and told her¦148419, “Now, please¦148422 put on mourning clothes¦148426 and don't¦148429 \add ≈put on any make-up\add*. \add ≈Act\add* like¦148434 a woman who¦148438 has¦148438 been¦148438 mourning for the¦148420 dead¦148441 for \add ≈several¦148437\add* days¦148436,
\v 3 and go¦148443 to the king and \add ≈give him¦148448 this¦148450 message¦148449\add*.” Then¦148443 Yoav¦148452 told her¦148456 what to say to the king.
\p
\v 4 \add ≈So¦148458\add* the Tekoan woman¦148459 went to the king¦148463 and¦148458 \add ≈fell¦148464 onto her¦148467 knees with his face¦148467 down¦148469 to the ground\add*, saying¦148458, “\add ≈Your majesty, help\add* \add me\add*.”
\p
\v 5 “What's¦148479 \add ≈the matter\add*?” the king¦148478 \add ≈asked\add*.
\p “Alas, I'm a¦148484 widow¦148486,” she¦148482 \add ≈replied¦148475\add*. “My¦148489 husband¦148489 has died¦148488.
\v 6 Your¦148491 female servant¦148491 had two sons¦148493, and the two of¦148495 them fought¦148494 \add each other out\add* in¦148496 the countryside¦148496. There¦148497 wasn't¦148497 anyone¦148501 there¦148497 who could \add ≈stop\add* them, and then¦148491 one¦148501 \add son\add* struck¦148500 the other and killed¦148505 him¦148500.
\v 7 \add ≈Now\add* listen, the entire¦148510 clan¦148512 has¦148509 \add ≈turned against\add* your¦148515 female servant¦148515 and \add ≈demanded\add*, ‘Give \add <us\add* the one¦148521 who¦148521 \add ≈killed\add* his¦148522 brother, and we'll kill¦148528 him¦148523 in¦148524 exchange for¦148524 the life¦148524 of¦148524 the brother that he¦148527 killed. Also¦148508, \add ≈it¦148509 would mean that this evil thing couldn't be passed on¦148524\add*.’ \add ≈But¦148508 that would leave¦148538 me with¦148524 no descendants to¦148539 continue\add* my¦148543 husband's¦148543 name¦148544.”
\p
\v 8 “Go¦148559 \add ≈home\add*,” the king¦148553 told the woman¦148556, “and¦148559 I'll¦148560 \add ≈make a decision about¦148558 what to¦148554 do\add*.”
