\v 9 \add ≈But¦148563\add* the Tekoan woman¦148564 \add ≈continued¦148563\add*, “The¦148565 \add ≈blame\add*,\f + \fr 14:9 \ft Presumably for not putting the murderer to death.\f* my master¦148570 the king, \add ≈will be on¦148569 me¦148569 and my extended family, but¦148563\add* the king and his¦148578 throne¦148578 will be innocent¦148579.”
\p
\v 10 “Anyone¦148584 who¦148584 speaks¦148584 against¦148591 you,” said¦148582 the¦148583 king¦148583, “bring¦148586 them to¦148587 me¦148587, and¦148588 then they won't¦148588 \add ≈trouble\add* you any more.”
