\v 13 \add ≈So\add* the woman¦148641 \add ≈asked\add*, “Why have¦148643 you¦148643 \add ≈acted\add* like¦148644 this¦148644 against God's¦148648 people¦148647? When the king¦148650 says¦148640 that¦148644 \add to me\add*, isn't¦148654 he convicting himself since he hasn't \add ≈brought¦148655 back¦148655\add* \em his¦148659 own\em* \add ≈banished¦148659 son¦148659\add*?
\v 14 \add ≈It's¦148680 certain¦148663 that we'll¦148664\add* \add all\add* die¦148663. Water¦148665 that's¦148666 spilt¦148666 on the ground can't¦148669 be gathered together \add again\add* \add ≈but¦148665\add* God's¦148674 \add not like that\add*. Rather than taking¦148673 away¦148673 life¦148675, he¦148673 devises¦148676 plans¦148677 so that the one who was banished¦148681 can be \add ≈gathered back in\add*.
\v 15 \add The reason\add* that¦148695 I've¦148686 come¦148686 now¦148683 to tell this¦148695 to the king my¦148691 master¦148691, is because¦148696 the people¦148698 have¦148697 frightened me¦148697. \add ≈So¦148683\add* your¦148700 servant said¦148699 \add to herself\add*, ‘I will speak¦148701, please¦148703, to the king. Perhaps¦148707 the king will \add ≈honour the request\add* of¦148712 his female servant.
\v 16 \add ≈Maybe\add* the king¦148717 will¦148716 listen¦148716 in order to¦148718 save his¦148721 female servant¦148721 from the man¦148723 who's \add ≈cutting\add* me¦148725 and¦148726 my¦148728 son¦148728 together¦148729 \add off\add* from the inheritance¦148730 given by God¦148731.’
\v 17 And your female servant¦148734 \add ≈thought\add*, ‘Please¦148737, let the word of¦148738 my master the king become¦148735 \add ≈my assurance\add*, because¦148743 my master the king is¦148747 like¦148745 God's¦148754 messenger¦148738 \add when it comes to\add* understanding good¦148751 and¦148733 evil. And may¦148755 Yahweh¦148740 your god¦148754 be¦148755 with¦148756 you¦148756.’ ”\x + \xo 14:17: \xt 2Sam 19:27.\x*
\p
\v 18 “\add Hang on,\add*” the king¦148760 told the woman¦148764. “\add ≈I¦148772 want you¦148774 to¦148762 answer¦148759 this question honestly\add*.”
\p “Please¦148767, let¦148777 my¦148780 master¦148780 the¦148760 king speak¦148777.” \add *she¦148775\add* \add ≈responded¦148761\add*.
\p
\v 19 “\add ≈Did Yoav¦148786 perhaps have anything to¦148803 do\add* with¦148819 all¦148788 this¦148790?” he¦148783 \add ≈asked\add*.
