\v 1 \add ≈During David's¦153404 reign\add*, there was¦153401 a¦153402 three-year¦153405 famine¦153402. David inquired from Yahweh¦153415 who said¦153417, “Sha'ul¦153421 \add ≈and¦153401 his family have blood¦153425 on¦153403 their hands\add*, because¦153419 he¦153401 killed the¦153403 Gibeonites.”
\v 2 (The Gibeonites were not¦153441 \add ≈native Israelis\add*, but were a remnant¦153448 of the Amorites¦153449. The Israelis had \add ≈promised¦153452 to protect them\add*, but Sha'ul¦153455 had attempted to \add ≈eliminate\add* them in¦153457 his zeal for¦153458 the people¦153458 of Yisrael¦153443 and Yehudah¦153461.) \add ≈So¦153435\add* the king¦153436 summoned the Gibeonites and \add ≈asked\add* them,\x + \xo 21:2: \xt Josh 9:3-15.\x*
\v 3 “What¦153468 can I do¦153469 for¦153470 all of¦153476 you? How¦153471 can I \add ≈remedy\add* \add what was done in the past\add* so that you all would bless¦153473 Yahweh's¦153477 \add ≈people\add*?”
